- [formats/interactions/tests/modal.test.ts](formats/interactions/tests/modal.test.ts) — test pattern with happy-dom, fakeTimers

### Generation & Build
- [formats/interactions/scripts/generate-capabilities.ts](formats/interactions/scripts/generate-capabilities.ts#L28) — hasBehavior() regex detection
- [formats/interactions/scripts/build-iife.ts](formats/interactions/scripts/build-iife.ts) — IIFE entry generation
- [formats/interactions/vite.config.ts](formats/interactions/vite.config.ts#L4) — ALL_COMPONENTS list, pack entry config
- [formats/interactions/component-capabilities.json](formats/interactions/component-capabilities.json) — auto-generated manifest (read-only during build)
- [formats/interactions/component-capabilities.schema.json](formats/interactions/component-capabilities.schema.json) — JSON schema for manifest

### Web Components (for reference)
- [renderers/web-components/src/elements/modal.ts](renderers/web-components/src/elements/modal.ts) — behavior integration in WC
- [renderers/web-components/src/elements/tooltip.ts](renderers/web-components/src/elements/tooltip.ts) — handle cleanup in disconnectedCallback

### Components Package (for reference)
- [formats/components/src/components/alert/alert.css](formats/components/src/components/alert/alert.css) — JSDoc @accessibility pattern

## Decision Questions for User

1. **Live Region Ownership**:
   - **Option A** (Auto-inject): initSkeletonLoader creates hidden role="status" region, auto-appended to document.body
     - Pro: Simple, works standalone
     - Con: Conflicts if parent already has live region
   - **Option B** (Parent-provided): Parent passes liveRegionRef to options, skeleton updates it
     - Pro: Parent controls placement, no conflicts
     - Con: Requires consumer setup
   - **Recommendation**: Option B + document in registry/guide as "consumer owns SSR-safe region"

2. **Capability Manifest Update**:
   - **Option A**: Hardcode skeleton-loader in generate-capabilities.ts with special handling
   - **Option B**: Move CSS from plugin to formats/components/skeleton-loader
   - **Recommendation**: Option A if keeping plugin pattern; requires documenting in AGENTS.md

3. **Auto-Register Scope** (skeleton-loader component file):
   - **Option A**: Full auto-init like modal/tooltip
     - Pro: Consistent with interactions pattern
     - Con: CSS-first consumers might not want JS
   - **Option B**: Manual registration only, parent calls initSkeletonLoader explicitly
     - Pro: Skeleton is CSS-first; JS is optional
     - Con: Breaks interactions convention
   - **Recommendation**: Option A (consistency), document that CSS works standalone

4. **Web Component Element**:
   - **Option A**: Add instui-skeleton-loader element in renderers/web-components
   - **Option B**: No web component, CSS only
   - **Recommendation**: Option A for feature parity, but document that CSS works standalone

5. **Error Announcement Role**:
   - Current proposal: Separate role="alert" region for errors, role="status" for loading
   - **Risk**: Two regions might duplicate in screen reader
   - **Recommendation**: Single role="status" region with aria-live="polite" for loads, switch to role="alert" only on error

## Summary: Minimal Consistent Pattern

**If approved**, the minimal pattern is:

1. **Skeleton CSS in custom-components** (already planned)
2. **initSkeletonLoader(target, { role, announceDelay, errorLabel })** in interactions/src/behaviors/ (NEW)
3. **Component auto-register** in interactions/src/components/skeleton-loader.ts (NEW)
4. **Vite pack entry** for skeleton-loader in interactions/vite.config.ts (NEW)
5. **Test** interactions/tests/skeleton-loader.test.ts (NEW)
6. **Capability manifest entry** auto-generated or hardcoded (NEW)
7. **Registry docs + demos** in docs/scripts/registry-plugins.ts + docs/demos/ (NEW)
8. **Consumer pattern** documented: real shell + SSR-initialized live region + delayed announce via updateState()

**No changes to**: components package, web-components package (optional WC addition), plugins/custom-components CSS
